A||||10||Shaft||Holden vs. M5 in Car & Driver||||10||
Z||000000||Shaft||08-20-2001||11:54 PM||||In the new Car & Driver they put the Holden Commadore With a performance package (Mods done by Calloway, 2 tone leather seats, and suspension mods) against am M5...and the Holden almost won!!! They said that the only things they didn't like about the Holden was the plasticy interior. They said it's one of the best cars GM has ever made...and we have no chance of getting it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I know a lot of people say this, including a lot of the mags, but this should be the next Camaro. I'd buy one for sure.  The two hottest cars GM could make in the US would be the Holden or the Pontiac Grand Prix G8 and unfortunately I don't think they're going to.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||08-21-2001||01:32 AM||||GM is redesigning their large car platform for 2005 (Impala, Bonneville, etc.) Maybe they'll get smart and build them right.<BR>Holden is also making a coupe that would make a great new Camaro or Firebird.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||08-21-2001||04:22 AM||||Just dump an LS1 into a Catera, that's what the car is.<P>Almost beating the M5 was a joke, even if it is the best car GM has ever made (and I think a very good thing) the M5 is in another leauge entirely.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Black88GT||08-21-2001||10:54 AM||||The C&D staff was very impressed with the Commodore.  To even put it up against an M5 says a lot to me, even if it did get beat.  <P>I heard that around 2004/2005 GM was going to start building all their sedans on this new "sigma" platform (i.e. commodore), which is going to be RWD (thank God!) like it should be.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-21-2001||11:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>...I heard that around 2004/2005 GM was going to start building all their sedans on this new "sigma" platform (i.e. commodore), which is going to be RWD (thank God!) like it should be.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One can only hope. I'd buy one in a heartbeat.<P>Aus posted a pic, a few weeks ago of a 2-door Holden. (Think it was a Monaro?) Rumor has it that it is going to be the basis for the new Camaro.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||08-21-2001||01:50 PM||||In that same issue, how many of you out there read the super tuner shootout, and started thinking to yourself:<P>If Aus designed the body, and Archie put in a LT1, and then we got some coilovers...<P>I think we could compete!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaft||08-21-2001||02:32 PM||||I read that Cadillac doesn't want anyone else to use the Sigma platform. They don't want to lose any prestige by someone saying that the Caddy and a Chevy are basically the same car. One scenero that was presented was that the Camaro would use a version of the Sigma platform dubbed the "sigma lite" that wouldn't be as stiff and would have a live rear axle instead of an independent rear suspension. Either way I think that would make a badass Camaro.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||08-21-2001||05:24 PM||||Shaft, yea I heard that too.  The 2003 Cadillac CTS is the first car sold in the U.S. with the new sigma platform.  All the mags love it, much better then the Catera.  Hopefully it will live up to expectations.  Like Raydar said, "I'd buy one in a heartbeat".<P>edited for spelling..<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||08-21-2001||07:11 PM||||The Sigma Lite chassis is just a 2 door version of the Sigma. Even if it doesn't turn up as a Camaro, Cadilac might use it. The Catera is smaller than a Commodore, the Commodore was designed seperately from the Omega (Catera) although it was based on the same platform (Not the sigma platform either, that just came out).||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||08-22-2001||07:48 AM||||The new Commodore Coupe...or Monaro, is rumoured in this country to be the replacement for the F-Body. It was not going to be made due to numbers then GM did a backflip.<P>It is supposed to be in the USA by 2005. By the rumours over here anyway.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Comcoupe01.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Comcoupe02.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||14
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||08-22-2001||01:57 PM||||To my knoweledge- the Catera IS on the same platform as the Commodore (ok... maybe it was the Calais), the Vauxhall Omega, the Opel Omega, and the Saturn L2000.  I'd gladly try to shoehorn an LS1 into a Catera- It would be great.<P>Last year on my honeymoon (in Scotland) we rented a Vauxhall Omega- it is one of the largest sedans in Britian and was running the biggest powerplant available on that model: a 2.2L Eco-Tec 4 cyl.  They don't even have the option of a V6 there.  Anyway, the Omega was a great ride and I survived right-side drive with only a parking ticket in Edinbourgh. Ever since I've been wanting the Catera and will buy one as soon as the money is available (which is quite a ways off if I keep dumping cash into the Fiero!)<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">       <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<P>Check this out! <A HREF="http://www.hsv.com.au/cars/vx/vx_clubsport/vx_clubsport_main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hsv.com.au/cars/vx/vx_clubsport/vx_clubsport_main.htm</A><P>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-22-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
